        <p>
<bold>Tier 2. Established Agents&#x000a0;</bold>
</p>
        <p>Agents that have demonstrated the ability to help achieve a 5% to 10% weight loss are categorized as tier 2, established pharmacologic therapies.</p>
        <p>
<bold>Liraglutide&#x000a0;</bold>
</p>
        <p>Liraglutide (Saxenda)<bold>&#x000a0;</bold>is a daily GLP-1 receptor agonist that pioneered incretin-based obesity therapy (see <bold>Table 3</bold>).&#x000a0;Please&#x000a0;refer to StatPearls' companion resource, "<ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://www.statpearls.com/point-of-care/120320">Pharmacologic Therapy for Obesity</ext-link>," for additional&#x000a0;information.&#x000a0;While offering more modest weight loss compared to newer weekly agents, liraglutide maintains clinical relevance through its established safety profile, pediatric indication for adolescents 12 years and older, and flexibility for dose adjustments. The SCALE clinical trial program demonstrated a 5.4% to 8.0% weight loss at 56 weeks, with 63.2% of participants achieving a weight loss of 5% or greater.</p>
