        <p>
<bold>Short-Acting Sympathomimetic Amines</bold>
</p>
        <p>Short-acting sympathomimetic amines represent a potential option in obesity management, though their use demands careful clinical consideration (see&#x000a0;<bold>Table 12</bold>). These agents stimulate the central nervous system to suppress appetite and increase energy expenditure, facilitating modest short-term weight loss. Their role remains limited, as data on long-term outcomes are insufficient to establish sustained efficacy.</p>
